# Dastro 3.3 — manual patch

## 1. Replace `normalizedIsoLocale` (optional in `'language'` mode)

Dastro 3.3 adds the `i18n.localePrefix` option and two helpers from `i18n()`
that follow it:

- `localePrefix(locale)` for URL prefixes (`/${localePrefix(locale)}`)
- `localeLangTag(locale)` for `<html lang>`, hreflang, tracking and form values

`normalizedIsoLocale` keeps working and, in the default `'language'` mode,
returns the same values. Nothing breaks if you leave it. Replace its calls
when you touch the code, and in any case before setting
`i18n.localePrefix: 'locale'`:

```sh
grep -rn normalizedIsoLocale src
```

- `normalizedIsoLocale(locale)` building a URL → `localePrefix(locale)`
- `normalizedIsoLocale(locale)` / `normalizedIsoLocale(locale, true)` as a
  language value → `localeLangTag(locale)`

See `node_modules/dastro/consumer-docs/i18n.md` for all new i18n options (`localePrefix`,
`xDefaultLocale`, `languageFallbacks`, `localeCookie`, per-locale noindex via
`_allSeoLocales`).

## 2. Root redirect (`routingStrategy: 'prefix-always'` only)

The redirect from `/` to a locale now:

- sorts `Accept-Language` entries by q-value and ignores `q=0`, `*` and
  malformed entries (browsers already send them sorted, so real visitors see
  no change)
- keeps the query string (`/?utm_source=x` → `/de/?utm_source=x`)
- is never cached, neither in the browser nor in the Netlify CDN

No action needed.
